Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat(floor-studio): the catalogue of floors Ecowoods can
 actually lay
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FS-01 of the Floor Studio series.

Floor Studio renders a floor into a photograph of somebody's living room.
The one thing that decides whether that is a product or a gimmick is
whether the floor in the picture can be bought and installed. Every
visualiser in this category fails that test: a generative model invents a
plank that exists nowhere, the homeowner falls in love with it, and the
sale cannot be fulfilled. So the first thing built is the boundary, not
the renderer.

lib/floor-studio/catalog.ts is that boundary. A configuration that is not
expressible here cannot be rendered, priced, shared or handed to the
estimate form.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CONTAIN

Prices. Not one figure. priceConfiguration() delegates to
estimateInstalledRangeCad() — the same function /design renders and the
same function /api/chat's estimate_project tool calls. A test asserts the
two are byte-identical for the same inputs, because a homeowner who sees
$14,200 on the page and hears $11,800 from the assistant has caught this
business lying about money.

Movement figures. movementFor() computes them on demand from lib/wood —
Wood Handbook Table 13-5 coefficients, the published EMC model, the board
width the visitor chose. A stored millimetre would be a claim nobody
could re-derive.

BOARD WIDTH IS A NEW AXIS AND IT DOES NOT TOUCH THE BAND

It was tempting to give width a price multiplier. The finish and pattern
multipliers in packages/shared/ai are already flagged in that file as
placeholders awaiting the estimator's confirmation; a third invented one
would deepen a debt this repository has already written down. What width
really changes is how the floor looks and how far each board moves
between a Toronto July and a Toronto February — and lib/wood can compute
the second from a published table. Both are true. A surcharge would not be.

COMPATIBILITY IS CHEMISTRY AND GEOMETRY

Fuming is an ammonia reaction with tannin, which is what the finish blurb
on /design already says; hard maple and hickory do not carry enough of it,
so they are not offered smoked. Herringbone and chevron are cut as blocks
and stop reading as a pattern past about five inches, so they are offered
at 3.25" and 5". Both constraints return a SENTENCE, not a boolean — a
control that silently disables itself teaches a visitor the product is
broken; one that explains the tannin teaches them something true.

withAxis() repairs the axis that broke and never the one the visitor just
moved, and reports what it repaired so the UI can narrate it.

/design NOW READS THE CATALOGUE

FloorConfigurator carried its own five species objects. Two lists of the
same five floors is how a visitor configures white oak in one surface and
meets a different white oak in another. The catalogue is now the record
and the configurator is a projection of it — ids stay the rate keys
('white oak', not 'white-oak') because that string is in every shared
/design link and in ew-design-v1 in people's browsers, and swatchNote
preserves the tooltip copy verbatim. The rendered page does not change.

24 tests. pnpm verify green (66 guards).

